global-distributor-of-telecoms-equipment-and-supplies/","evidence":"Permira Debt Managers (“PDM”), one of Europe’s leading specialist debt investors, today announces that funds it advises are acting as senior secured lender in The Carlyle Group’s acquisition of Euro Techno Com (“ETC”).","verified":null},{"key":"pr:4a4c29c16671e329e4877bfeb0ae6494","date":"2019-09-05","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Axiom","portco_name":"Axiom","target_website":"axiomlaw.com","investor":"Permira","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Axiom Announces Strategic Investment from the Permira Funds","summary":"Axiom entered into a definitive agreement for a Permira-backed company to make a significant investment in the on-demand legal talent provider.","source_name":"Permira","source_url":"https://www.permira.com/news-and-insights/announcements/axiom-announces-strategic-investment-from-the-permira-funds/","evidence":"Axiom, the global leader in specialized on-demand legal talent, and Permira, the global private equity firm, today announced that they have entered into a definitive agreement whereby a company backed by the Permira funds will make a significant investment in Axiom.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:b4ed08c1b610241255605f35074b91b9","date":"2019-09-04","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Topcast","portco_name":"Topcast","target_website":"topcast.com","investor":"Permira","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Founders of Topcast","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Permira announces buyout of Topcast, APAC’s leading independent aircraft parts distributor","summary":"A Permira-backed company agreed to buy a majority of Asia-Pacific aircraft parts distributor Topcast from its founders.","source_name":"Permira","source_url":"https://www.permira.com/news-and-insights/announcements/permira-announces-buyout-of-topcast-apac-s-leading-independent-aircraft-parts-distributor/","evidence":"Global investment firm Permira today announced that a company backed by the Permira Funds will acquire the majority of the shares of Topcast Aviation Supplies Company Limited and its affiliates (“Topcast” or “the Company”), the largest independent aircraft parts distributor in the Asia Pacific region, from its founders.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:a7918c7bdce4944652e46709dd34fd94","date":"2019-08-18","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Cambrex","portco_name":"Cambrex","target_website":"cambrex.com","investor":"Permira","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":2400000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Cambrex to be Acquired by the Permira Funds for $60.00 per Share in Cash","summary":"Cambrex agreed to be acquired by an affiliate of the Permira funds for $60.00 per share in a deal valued at about $2.4bn including net debt.","source_name":"Permira","source_url":"https://www.permira.com/news-and-insights/announcements/cambrex-to-be-acquired-by-the-permira-funds-for-6000-per-share-in-cash/","evidence":"announced today that it has signed a definitive agreement to be acquired by an affiliate of the Permira funds in a transaction valued at approximately $2.4 billion, including Cambrex’s net debt","verified":true},{"key":"pr:843e0055261e04e2c0ce4d0e0a4cf49c","date":"2019-07-19","date_text":null,"kind":"funding_round","asset_class":"venture_capital","target":"FlixMobility","portco_name":"FlixMobility","target_website":"flix.com","investor":"TCV","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["Permira","HV Holtzbrinck Ventures","European Investment Bank"],"seller":null,"round":"Series F","stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"FlixMobility Completes New Funding Round Led by TCV and Permira","summary":"FlixMobility (FlixBus, FlixTrain) completed a Series F round co-led by TCV and Permira, with HV Holtzbrinck Ventures and the European Investment Bank participating.","source_name":"Permira","source_url":"https://www.permira.com/news-and-insights/announcements/flixmobility-completes-new-funding-round-led-by-tcv-and-permira/","evidence":"FlixMobility GmbH, the parent company of global mobility platforms FlixBus and FlixTrain, has announced the completion of its Series F funding round co-led by TCV and Permira, two of the largest growth equity firms backing private and public technology companies.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:b67ecdab8087770c5eb708215d80fbe9","date":"2019-07-18","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Quotient Sciences","portco_name":"Quotient Sciences","target_website":"quotientsciences.com","investor":"Permira","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"GHO Capital","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Quotient Sciences to Recapitalize With Global Private Equity Firm Permira","summary":"A Permira-backed company agreed to acquire a majority stake in drug development accelerator Quotient Sciences from GHO Capital and other investors for an undisclosed sum.","source_name":"Permira","source_url":"https://www.permira.com/news-and-insights/announcements/quotient-sciences-to-recapitalize-with-global-private-equity-firm-permira/","evidence":"Quotient Sciences and global investment firm Permira today announced that a company backed by the Permira Funds has signed a definitive agreement to acquire a majority stake in Quotient from companies controlled by GHO Capital and other investors for an undisclosed sum.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7a7eecdc149aec795a3d6d608d3da10e","date":"2019-07-10","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Reformation","portco_name":"Reformation","target_website":"thereformation.com","investor":"Permira","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Sustainable fashion brand Reformation announces majority investment from the Permira Funds","summary":"A Permira-backed company agreed to acquire a majority stake in sustainable fashion brand Reformation; founder Yael Aflalo remains a significant owner.","source_name":"Permira","source_url":"https://www.permira.com/news-and-insights/announcements/sustainable-fashion-brand-reformation-announces-majority-investment-from-the-permira-funds/","evidence":"Reformation, the premier sustainable fashion brand, and Permira, the global private equity firm, today announced that a company backed by the Permira funds has entered into a definitive agreement to acquire a majority stake in Reformation.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:0a296ef96f9852e3c8f339f0ce4c7070","date":"2019-06-17","date_text":null,"kind":"add_on_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"LSNE-León (sterile injectables facility, León, Spain)","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"LSNE","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"LSNE establishes presence in Europe through acquisition of sterile injectables manufacturing facility located in León, Spain","summary":"Permira-backed LSNE acquired a sterile injectables manufacturing facility in León, Spain, establishing its presence in Europe.","source_name":"Permira","source_url":"https://www.permira.com/news-and-insights/announcements/lsne-establishes-presence-in-europe-through-acquisition-of-sterile-injectables-manufacturing-facility-located-in-leon-spain/","evidence":"Lyophilization Services of New England (LSNE), a leading contract development and manufacturing organization (CDMO), announced today the acquisition of a sterile injectables manufacturing facility located in León, Spain.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:957c0ab1f55dd0e336d5ace6f3e55fbf","date":"2019-05-08","date_text":null,"kind":"add_on_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Richful Deyong","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"Tricor","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Tricor Accelerates China Outbound Business with Acquisition of Richful Deyong","summary":"Permira-backed Tricor acquired Hong Kong corporate services provider Richful Deyong.","source_name":"Permira","source_url":"https://www.permira.com/news-and-insights/announcements/tricor-accelerates-china-outbound-business-with-acquisition-of-richful-deyong/","evidence":"Tricor Group(Tricor), Asia’s leading provider of business, corporate, investor and debt administration services, has acquired Richful Deyong (RFDY), a Hong Kong-based provider of integrated corporate and business services, focused on supporting mainland Chinese companies in their international corporate activities.","verified":null}]}$pf$::jsonb;
  n_companies int;
  n_deals int;
begin
  select id into gp from public.companies
   where category = 'GP' and name = 'Permira'
   order by (source = 'master_directory') desc nulls last, created_at
   limit 1;
  if gp is null then raise exception 'sponsor % is not in the directory', 'Permira'; end if;

  insert into public.portfolio_companies as pc (external_key, gp_company_id, name, domain, description, sector, hq, status, invested_year, exit_year, fund_name,
      source, source_url, deal_value, deal_currency, deal_value_basis, stake_pct, co_investors, deal_source_url, researched_at)
  select gp::text || ':' || (c->>'slug'), gp, c->>'name', c->>'domain', c->>'description', c->>'sector', c->>'hq', c->>'status',
         (c->>'invested_year')::int, (c->>'exit_year')::int, c->>'fund_name', 'web_research', c->>'source_url',
         (c->>'deal_value')::numeric, c->>'deal_currency', c->>'deal_value_basis', (c->>'stake_pct')::numeric,
         coalesce(array(select jsonb_array_elements_text(c->'co_investors')), '{}'), c->>'deal_source_url', now()
    from jsonb_array_elements(doc->'companies') c
  on conflict (external_key) do update set
    name = case when pc.source = 'manual' then pc.name else excluded.name end,
    domain = coalesce(pc.domain, excluded.domain),
    description = case when pc.source = 'manual' then coalesce(pc.description, excluded.description) else coalesce(excluded.description, pc.description) end,
    sector = case when pc.source = 'manual' then coalesce(pc.sector, excluded.sector) else coalesce(excluded.sector, pc.sector) end,
    hq = case when pc.source = 'manual' then coalesce(pc.hq, excluded.hq) else coalesce(excluded.hq, pc.hq) end,
    status = coalesce(excluded.status, pc.status),
    invested_year = coalesce(excluded.invested_year, pc.invested_year),
    exit_year = coalesce(excluded.exit_year, pc.exit_year),
    fund_name = coalesce(excluded.fund_name, pc.fund_name),
    source_url = case when pc.source = 'manual' then coalesce(pc.source_url, excluded.source_url) else excluded.source_url end,
    deal_value = coalesce(excluded.deal_value, pc.deal_value),
    deal_currency = case when excluded.deal_value is not null then excluded.deal_currency else pc.deal_currency end,
    deal_value_basis = case when excluded.deal_value is not null then excluded.deal_value_basis else pc.deal_value_basis end,
    stake_pct = coalesce(excluded.stake_pct, pc.stake_pct),
    co_investors = case when cardinality(excluded.co_investors) > 0 then excluded.co_investors else pc.co_investors end,
    deal_source_url = coalesce(excluded.deal_source_url, pc.deal_source_url),
    researched_at = now();
  get diagnostics n_companies = row_count;

  insert into public.deals as d (external_key, date, date_text, kind, asset_class, target, target_kind, target_key, target_website, investor, investor_company_id,
      co_investors, seller, round, stake_pct, amount, currency, amount_basis, valuation, valuation_currency, headline, summary, source_name, source_url,
      evidence, verified, source)
  select x->>'key', (x->>'date')::date, x->>'date_text', x->>'kind', x->>'asset_class', x->>'target', 'company',
         public.borrower_key(coalesce(x->>'portco_name', x->>'target')), x->>'target_website', x->>'investor',
         case when (x->>'sponsor_is_investor')::boolean then gp else (select m.company_id from ingest.match_firm(x->>'investor', array['GP']) m) end,
         coalesce(array(select jsonb_array_elements_text(x->'co_investors')), '{}'), x->>'seller', x->>'round', (x->>'stake_pct')::numeric,
         (x->>'amount')::numeric, x->>'currency', x->>'amount_basis', (x->>'valuation')::numeric, x->>'valuation_currency',
         x->>'headline', x->>'summary', x->>'source_name', x->>'source_url', x->>'evidence', (x->>'verified')::boolean, 'web_research'
    from jsonb_array_elements(doc->'deals') x
  on conflict (external_key) do update set
    date = excluded.date, date_text = excluded.date_text, kind = excluded.kind, target = excluded.target, target_key = excluded.target_key,
    target_website = coalesce(excluded.target_website, d.target_website), investor = excluded.investor,
    investor_company_id = coalesce(excluded.investor_company_id, d.investor_company_id),
    co_investors = (select coalesce(array_agg(distinct v), '{}') from unnest(d.co_investors || excluded.co_investors) v),
    seller = coalesce(excluded.seller, d.seller), round = coalesce(excluded.round, d.round), stake_pct = coalesce(excluded.stake_pct, d.stake_pct),
    amount = excluded.amount, currency = excluded.currency, amount_basis = excluded.amount_basis,
    valuation = excluded.valuation, valuation_currency = excluded.valuation_currency, headline = excluded.headline,
    summary = coalesce(excluded.summary, d.summary), source_name = excluded.source_name, source_url = excluded.source_url,
    evidence = excluded.evidence, verified = coalesce(excluded.verified, d.verified);
  get diagnostics n_deals = row_count;

  update public.companies set portfolio_note = 'permira.com portfolio JSON endpoint /api/portfolio?page=N&filters={"status":["current"|"realised"]} (110 companies) + per-company /api/page?path=/portfolio/our-portfolio/<slug>/ for sector, HQ, years, website; plus 694 Permira announcements via /api/news (deals not on the portfolio list) and public record (Wikipedia, press) for older realised deals; invested_year for 16 site companies without a st', portfolio_researched_at = now() where id = gp;
  insert into ingest.log (what, detail) values ('load_portfolio', jsonb_build_object('sponsor', 'Permira', 'companies', n_companies, 'deals', n_deals));
end $pfdo$;
